    "narrative": "The Austin Waves project for a balanced offensive output today, anchored by the premium matchup for **Gunnar Henderson** (74.74) against J.T. Soriano. **Gunnar Henderson** remains our most efficient play, buoyed by a strong #2 spot in the order and a favorable dynamic platoon advantage. **Josh Lowe** (69.57) and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (66.91) also emerge as high-ceiling options, with **Josh Lowe** specifically benefiting from a soft matchup against Kyle Gibson\u2014the high expected ERA (5.27) of the opposing starter provides an ideal environment for **Josh Lowe** to capitalize on his power-speed profile. Meanwhile, **Nolan Schanuel** (64.83) continues to offer reliable efficiency, utilizing his leadoff positioning to maximize run-scoring opportunities in what looks like a volatile but high-upside contest against Gibson.\n\nThe most difficult exclusion today was **Jacob Wilson** (57.24), who narrowly missed the cut behind the stability of **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** and **Curtis Mead**. While **Jacob Wilson** received a minor boost from favorable wind conditions, the optimizer favored the consistent platoon-neutral upside of our middle infield block. Owners should exercise caution regarding the rain risk (32%) currently hanging over **Sam Antonacci** and **Brayan Rocchio**. Additionally, the efficiency of **Kyle Tucker** (53.12) is severely suppressed by a challenging matchup against Joe Ryan; despite his elite pedigree, he is a \"marginal\" start today due to the SP skill delta. We will continue to monitor the \"Lineup Pending\" status for **Drake Baldwin**, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, **Curtis Mead**, **Jackson Merrill**, and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** to ensure our lineup optimizations hold against final configurations.",
